{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-color-tube-fibers","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:color-tube-fibers","kind":"definition","title":"Color tube fibers","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-color-tube-cubic"],"tags":["brings-surface","color-tube"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ColorTubeFibers","text":"color-tube-fibers.md","leanSource":"color-tube-fibers.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:color-tube-fibers\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z \\in \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code>. The <strong>color tube</strong> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z</code> is the zero-dimensional subscheme of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{A}^1</code> defined over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[z]</code> by the color tube cubic; for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z</code> off the branch locus it consists of three points. It is denoted <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R_z</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_z</code>, or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_z</code> according to which color tube coordinate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{r}_z</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{g}_z</code>, or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{b}_z</code> is used:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">R_z  := \n  \\bigl\\{\\mathbf{r}_z \\in \\mathbb{A}^1 :\n    \\mathbf{r}_z^{3} + (4z+1)\\mathbf{r}_z^{2}\n    + (6z^2+3z+1)\\mathbf{r}_z\n    + (4z^3+3z^2+2z+1) = 0\\bigr\\}.</code></pre>\n<p>The curves <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_z</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_z</code> are defined by the same equation with coordinates <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{g}_z</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{b}_z</code>, respectively. The coordinates relate to the Lagrange resolvents by</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathbf{r}_z = w_2 - z, \\qquad \\mathbf{g}_z = w_3 - z, \\qquad\n  \\mathbf{b}_z = w_4 - z.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.md","heading":"Definition","number":"8.6.4","page":"b/def-color-tube-fibers","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.ColorTubeFibers","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
